he forces my intent was never to  make this public or widely known she  said  it was for the minister to deal with it  at an appropriate time  and perhaps reconsider how operation  honor was commanded  a time the woman thought like when the  government was deciding on the general's  future  including extending his term the trudeau  government made  vance canada's longest serving chief of  the defense staff he remained in office  for almost three years after the  concerns  were brought forward the liberal  government has defended its lack of  action  saying it couldn't proceed without the  name of the woman  but she says she asked the ombudsman to  protect her identity  and thought the email would be proof  enough for the minister and  others mercedes stevenson global news  ottawa  ahead the variant first detected in  india lands in canada what's being done  to  reduce the risk of its spreading  the variant first detected in india is  now in canada quebec has identified  what's believed to be the first  confirmed case in the country  it's not clear how it got here but there  are still daily flights between india  and canada  and there's concern the variant is  fueling a terrible fourth wave  in india redmond shannon reports  another virus victim  another morning family parts of india  are in the grip of a covid19 crisis  hospitals are short on beds and oxygen  this hospital oxygen leak is being  blamed for  22 patient deaths crematoriums are  working  around the clock and the capital is  among regions currently in lockdown  for months cases dropped in india  leading some to think it had achieved a  type of  herd immunity a naive assumption for a  mutating virus according to dr prabhu  the  sense that the first infection would  take care  and immunize the population really  hasn't occurred  researchers are still trying to  establish whether the b1617 variant  first found in india and now in canada  is more infectious it's undoubtable  that the big spike that's occurring now  is because of these variants  you see them occurring in younger  population you see them occurring in  different geographic areas  ja says it's likely there are more cases  of the variant in canada  that haven't yet been detected i think  there are slightly over 100  such cases that we've identified here in  the in the uk  the uk is about to ban airport arrivals  for all foreigners who've recently been  in india i have asked our officials  to look carefully at for example what  the uk has done  very recently on suspending flights from  india but for now prime minister justin  trudeau says  airport testing and quarantine measures  are effective  in reducing the risk of importing new  variants  not all experts agree personally now  looking into the situation we're in  right now we can't wait for conclusive  evidence  right now the precautionary principle  will tell you  you need to react the better news is  that the specific mutations in b1617  suggest  vaccines should work against the variant  redmond shannon global news london  next a guilty verdict delivers hope for  racial justice in george floyd city  for 11 months the spot on the street  where george floyd took his final  breaths has been ground zero for grief  and outrage  president biden said yesterday his  murder here in the full light of day  ripped the blinders off for the whole  world to see  the systemic racism in america people  have occupied george floyd square to  keep up the pressure for racial justice  and police reform  and as heather urex west reports the  struggle is far from over  for nearly a year the mood in  minneapolis has  been heavy there has been sadness there  has been rage  and this week there has been a lot of  anxiety too  there has just been this tense  you know pregnant feeling in the air  since the jury began its deliberation  so when the verdict came down the sense  of relief was  overwhelming when i heard the verdict i  just screamed and i shouted and i said  thank you guys  last night when i got home i think i was  sleeping for nine  jamar nelson listened to the verdict  from the crowd outside of  court i had knots in my stomach because  i you know again i  i i was hoping that he got convicted on  the third degree  and the manslaughter um was not  anticipating  that he would be convicted on all three  counts but nelson knows  there is still so much work left to be  done  will the derrick chovin's trial was  taking place in nearby brooklyn center  another black man  20-year-old dante wright was killed by  another member of the police  kim potter has been charged with second  degree murder  she too should face faced justice  and the arm of the law the murder of  george floyd sparked global protests  as painful as his final moments were to  watch they were also  impossible to ignore i'd say overall  this verdict feels like a brief bit of  relief  right it feels like a measure of  accountability  which many people doubted could happen  here but palmisano admits in minneapolis  nothing has been fixed  the city is still grappling with how its  police department should be reformed  still the importance of this moment in  time  cannot be discounted these things help  because now it can incur you can now  encourage  our black and brown boys and girls to  become officers to change  to be the chains that they want to be  and so  while there is no joy with this verdict  there  is hope heather urex west global news  calgary and that is global national for  this wednesday i'm donna friesen  this is queen elizabeth ii's birthday  she turns 95 today  but there is no celebration it has been  just four days since the funeral of her  husband prince philip  buckingham palace released a photo in a  statement thanking people for the many  good wishes and saying  well as a family we are in a period of  great sadness it has been a comfort to  us all to see  and to hear the tributes paid to my  husband  thanks for watching take care of  yourselves bye-bye  